# oracle: ReaxFF water (55 molecules cut from examples/reaxff/water data.water) with fix qtpie/reaxff (Gaussian overlap chi_eff, tolerance 1e-8, gauss_exp.txt), energy minimization (cg, 20 iterations), thermo at every iteration, atoms at the end
# oracle-inputs: w65reaxq_water.data w65reaxq_qeq_ff.water w65reaxq_gauss_exp.txt
# Measured with native LAMMPS (20 CG iterations, 21 rows, max relative error): Node 24 press 3.0e-6 (last row), atoms 1.6e-6 (fx); Node 20 press 3.5e-7, atoms 1.3e-6 (fx); pe 2e-11 and 2.5e-11.
# Press is small near the end of the minimization, so its error is the largest column; compared at rel=1e-5.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-5 abs=1e-8
units           real
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
read_data       w65reaxq_water.data
pair_style      reaxff NULL safezone 3.0 mincap 150
pair_coeff      * * w65reaxq_qeq_ff.water O H
fix             1 all qtpie/reaxff 1 0.0 10.0 1e-8 reaxff w65reaxq_gauss_exp.txt
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
thermo_style    custom step pe ebond evdwl ecoul press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          1
minimize        1.0e-8 1.0e-8 20 100
